{"title":"Career roadmap · Deck Cadet","role":"Deck Cadet","summary":"A Deck Cadet is an entry-level officer trainee on a merchant vessel who assists the deck department with navigation, cargo operations, watchkeeping, safety, seamanship, maintenance and shipboard procedures.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Merchant Navy – Maritime Science","Timeline assumption":"3-year B.Sc/nautical-science pathway is common, but programme structure varies by institution. Verify the current DG Shipping-approved route before admission."},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Direct"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a highly regulated career: academic study alone is not enough. A candidate generally needs the appropriate maritime education, medical fitness, required safety training, approved sea service and certification/CoC progression under the applicable maritime authority."}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Maritime/Nautical Science","approved pre-sea training","Deck Cadet","required sea service + assessments","Second Mate / Officer of the Watch","Chief Officer","Master (Captain)"]},{"type":"p","text":"In India, check the current requirements and approved institutes through Directorate General of Shipping (DG Shipping).","url":"https://www.dgshipping.gov.in/"}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What to focus on"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Complete maritime education, mandatory safety training and structured sea-time requirements."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Progress from Deck Cadet toward Officer of the Watch/Second Mate certification."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Build experience toward Chief Officer responsibilities."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Master/Captain or shore-