vention"},{"text":"Bridge Watchkeeping"},{"text":"Radar & ARPA"},{"text":"ECDIS"},{"text":"GMDSS"},{"text":"Maritime Security"},{"text":"Leadership & Teamwork"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Navigation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nautical charts"},{"text":"Position fixing"},{"text":"Compass work"},{"text":"Passage planning"},{"text":"Radar"},{"text":"ARPA"},{"text":"ECDIS"},{"text":"GPS/GNSS"},{"text":"AIS"},{"text":"COLREGs"},{"text":"Meteorological information"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Deck operations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mooring"},{"text":"Anchoring"},{"text":"Cargo handling"},{"text":"Lashing"},{"text":"Ship maintenance"},{"text":"Rigging"},{"text":"Deck machinery"},{"text":"Watchkeeping"},{"text":"Safety rounds"},{"text":"Emergency drills"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fire prevention/fighting"},{"text":"Personal survival techniques"},{"text":"Elementary first aid"},{"text":"Personal safety and social responsibility"},{"text":"Security awareness"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"Pollution prevention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn from","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"ECDIS, radar, ARPA, passage planning"},{"text":"Bridge simulator + sea service"},{"text":"Chief Officer/Master"}],[{"text":"Cargo Operations"},{"text":"Cargo planning, stability, securing"},{"text":"Vessel cargo operations"},{"text":"Chief Officer"}],[{"text":"Tanker Operations"},{"text":"Oil/chemical/LNG cargo systems"},{"text":"Approved tanker training"},{"text":"Senior Tanker Officer"}],[{"text":"Container Shipping"},{"text":"Container planning, lashing, stability"},{"text":"Container vessels"},{"text":"Chief Officer"}],[{"text":"Bulk Carriers"},{"text":"Bulk cargo handling, IMSBC concepts"},{"text":"Bulk shipping"},{"text":"Chief Officer"}],[{"text":"Offshore Maritime"},{"text":"DP/offshore operations"},{"text":"Offshore training"},{"text":"Offshore Deck Officer"}],[{"text":"Maritime Safety"},{"text":"ISM, emergency management"},{"text":"Shipboard safety systems"},{"text":"Safety Superintendent"}],[{"text":"Maritime Operations"},{"text":"Fleet operations, compliance"},{"text":"Shipping companies"},{"text":"Marine Superintendent"}],[{"text":"Maritime Logistics"},{"text":"Cargo, ports, supply chain"},{"text":"Port/shipping organisations"},{"text":"Port/Marine Operations Manager"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Evolve and stay relevant, 2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern deck officers increasingly work with ECDIS, integrated bridge systems, digital voyage planning, satellite communications, electronic documentation, automation, remote monitoring and increasingly data-driven fleet operations. Future officers should also understand cyber-security, environmental regulations, alternative fuels and decarbonisation."}]},{"heading":"Internships / sea training","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For this career, structured sea training is more important than a conventional office internship."},{"type":"h","text":"Key organisations and pathways"},{"type":"table","header":["Organisation","Relevant exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Directorate General of Shipping (DG Shipping)","url":"https://www.dgshipping.gov.in/"},{"text":"Indian maritime regulation, approved institutes and certification"}],[{"text":"Indian Maritime University","url":"https://www.imu.edu.in/"},{"text":"Maritime education and training"}],[{"text":"DG Shipping-approved maritime institutes"},{"text":"Pre-sea education and training"}],[{"text":"Shipping companies"},{"text":"Cadetship and sea-time opportunities"}],[{"text":"Ship-management companies"},{"text":"Vessel operations and cadet placement"}],[{"text":"Port operators"},{"text":"Port and cargo operations"}],[{"text":"Classification societies"},{"text":"Maritime safety/compliance exposure"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Shipping companies to monitor"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"The Shipping Corporation of India","url":"https://www.shipindia.com/"},{"text":"Anglo-Eastern","url":"https://www.angloeastern.com/"},{"text":"Synergy Marine Group","url":"https://www.synergyship.com/"},{"text":"Fleet Management Limited","url":"https://www.fleetship.com/"},{"text":"Bernhard Schulte Shipmanagement","url":"https://www.bs-shipmanagement.com/"},{"text":"Maersk","url":"https://www.maersk.com/"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["A properly documented Training Record Book","qualifying sea service","approved training certificates","strong performance reports."],"sep":"+","label":"Best evidence"}]},{"heading":"Certifications in demand","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Certification/course","Cost","When","Why it helps"],"rows":[[{"text":"STCW Basic Safety Training"},{"text":"Paid; current fee: check the official site"},{"text":"Before/around sea training"},{"text":"Mandatory maritime safety foundation"}],[{"text":"Personal Survival Techniques"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Pre-sea"},{"text":"Emergency survival"}],[{"text":"Fire Prevention & Fire Fighting"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Pre-sea"},{"text":"Fire response"}],[{"text":"Elementary First Aid"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Pre-sea"},{"text":"Medical emergency response"}],[{"text":"Personal Safety & Social Responsibility"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Pre-sea"},{"text":"Shipboard safety"}],[{"text":"Security Awareness"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Pre-sea"},{"text":"Maritime security"}],[{"text":"GMDSS-related training"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Officer pathway"},{"text":"Maritime communications"}],[{"text":"Radar/ARPA"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Officer pathway"},{"text":"Navigation"}],[{"text":"ECDIS"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Officer pathway"},{"text":"Electronic navigation"}],[{"text":"Advanced Fire Fighting"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Officer progression"},{"text":"Advanced emergency response"}],[{"text":"Advanced First Aid/Medical Care"},{"text":"Course-dependent"},{"text":"Officer progression"},{"text":"Shipboard medical response"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Do not pay an institute until you confirm that the specific course/institute is currently approved by DG Shipping and that its qualification leads to the certification you need."},{"type":"p","text":"The international framework is governed primarily through the STCW Convention under International Maritime Organization (IMO).","url":"https://www.imo.org/"}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"First-job targets"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Deck Cadet"},{"text":"Nautical Cadet"},{"text":"Trainee Deck Officer"},{"text":"Deck Trainee"},{"text":"Junior Deck Officer (only after meeting applicable certification requirements)"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career progression"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Typical progression requirement","Proof of capability"],"rows":[[{"text":"Deck Cadet"},{"text":"Approved education + training + sea placement"},{"text":"Training Record Book"}],[{"text":"Third Officer / OOW"},{"text":"Required sea service + competency certification"},{"text":"CoC"}],[{"text":"Second Officer"},{"text":"Officer experience + company progression"},{"text":"Sea-service record"}],[{"text":"Chief Officer"},{"text":"Higher certification + required sea time"},{"text":"Management-level CoC"}],[{"text":"Master/Captain"},{"text":"Master-level certification + experience"},{"text":"Master CoC"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Shore-based alternatives later"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Marine Superintendent"},{"text":"Fleet Operations Executive"},{"text":"Marine Safety Officer"},{"text":"Port Operations Executive"},{"text":"Ship Management Executive"},{"text":"Marine Surveyor"},{"text":"Marine Compliance Executive"},{"text":"Marine Training Instructor"},{"text":"Maritime Logistics Manager"},{"text":"Marine Claims/Operations Executive"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Postgraduate study is not required to become a deck officer. The priority is completing the approved maritime training and competency pathway."},{"type":"p","text":"However, later-career options include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Route","Entrance","Examples","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"MBA Maritime Management"},{"text":"University/institute-specific"},{"text":"Maritime-management institutions"},{"text":"Shipping management"}],[{"text":"MBA Port & Shipping Management"},{"text":"Institute-specific"},{"text":"Relevant universities"},{"text":"Ports + shipping"}],[{"text":"M.Sc Maritime Studies"},{"text":"University-specific"},{"text":"Maritime universities"},{"text":"Maritime research/management"}],[{"text":"M.Sc Maritime Safety"},{"text":"University-specific"},{"text":"Relevant institutions"},{"text":"Safety/compliance"}],[{"text":"MBA Logistics & Supply Chain"},{"text":"CAT/other institute routes"},{"text":"IIMs + universities"},{"text":"Logistics"}],[{"text":"LL.M Maritime Law"},{"text":"Institution-specific"},{"text":"Law universities"},{"text":"Maritime legal work"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For maritime education, monitor Indian Maritime University and DG Shipping requirements.","url":"https://www.imu.edu.in/"}]},{"heading":"Study abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Example institutions","Scholarship route","Gate to check"],"rows":[[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"University of Southampton, Solent University"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Maritime qualification recognition"}],[{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Delft University of Technology, maritime institutions"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Programme requirements"}],[{"text":"Norway"},{"text":"University of South-Eastern Norway"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Maritime programme eligibility"}],[{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Australian Maritime College / University of Tasmania"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Maritime authority requirements"}],[{"text":"Singapore"},{"text":"Singapore maritime institutions"},{"text":"Institution-specific"},{"text":"Maritime certification recognition"}],[{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Memorial University and maritime institutions"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Programme requirements"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Application pack"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maritime academic transcript"},{"text":"STCW certificates"},{"text":"Medical fitness documentation"},{"text":"Sea-service records"},{"text":"Training Record Book"},{"text":"CoC/competency documentation where applicable"},{"text":"English-language test where required"},{"text":"CV"},{"text":"Employer references"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"If the goal is to work onboard an internationally trading vessel, check recognition of the qualification and CoC by the relevant flag state and maritime authority."}]},{"heading":"Going forward","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Maritime Science","Pre-Sea Training","Deck Cadet","Third Officer/OOW","Second Officer","Chief Officer","Master/Captain"]},{"type":"p","text":"A parallel shore route can be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Deck Cadet","Officer","Chief Officer","Marine Superintendent","Fleet Manager","Marine Operations Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research / advanced areas"},{"type":"p","text":"For a long-term academic or technical route:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maritime Safety"},{"text":"Navigation Systems"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Maritime Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Autonomous Shipping"},{"text":"Ship Operations"},{"text":"Maritime Logistics"},{"text":"Port Management"},{"text":"Marine Environmental Management"},{"text":"Alternative Marine Fuels"},{"text":"Decarbonisation"},{"text":"Digital Shipping"},{"text":"Vessel Performance Analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"By this stage, an experienced deck officer can choose between remaining at sea and progressing toward Master/Captain, or transitioning ashore into fleet management, marine safety, ship management, port operations, maritime training, compliance or maritime consulting. Digital navigation, autonomous vessels, alternative fuels and maritime cybersecurity will increasingly influence senior maritime roles."}]}]}